@startuml activity-fr-18-refund
' Report §2.1 — FR-18, the requestRefund tool (detail of activity-fr-18-tools.puml).
' Source: SupportTools.requestRefund, RefundGuard.evaluate, RequestedRefund, RestPaymentClient,
' RestRegistrationClient, UpstreamResults.
!include include/style.iuml
!include include/activity.iuml

title FR-18 — The requestRefund tool

|concierge-service|
start
:the model calls requestRefund(registrationId, reason);
:ownership guard as above;
if (already requested in this conversation,
or an earlier refund's outcome unknown?) then (yes)
  :refused;
else (no)
  :fetch a fresh quote — payment-service:
  GET /api/v1/refund-policy/quote;
  :RefundGuard.evaluate(quote, already requested);
  if (ineligible, zero, more than
  paid, another currency, or the
  conversation total above 200.00 AUD
  (refund-auto-approve-threshold)?) then (yes)
    :refused: "call escalateToOrganiser";
  else (no)
    :registration-service:
    POST /api/v1/registrations/{id}/
    refund-requests {reason,
    requestedBy AGENT} (FR-11);
    if (answer?) then (202)
      :record RequestedRefund;
    elseif (4xx) then (yes)
      :explain the refusal (e.g. 409 not confirmed);
    else (no answer)
      :outcome UNKNOWN — do not retry;
    endif
  endif
endif
:the result is returned to the model;
stop
note right
  The refund limit is code, not prompt:
  requestRefund fetches its own quote and
  RefundGuard judges the conversation's total.
end note
@enduml
